  "evidence": [
    "Every START_SECTION of NoopMSDataConsumer_test.cpp, MSDataStoringConsumer_test.cpp, MSDataTransformingConsumer_test.cpp, MSDataChainingConsumer_test.cpp, MSDataAggregatingConsumer_test.cpp and IndexedMzMLFileLoader_test.cpp is transcribed with its line numbers (source review, tier 3). No C++ was executed.",
    "MSDataSqlConsumer has no upstream class test; tests/ms_data_sql_consumer.rs derives every expectation from MSDataSqlConsumer.cpp, the central one being that streamed records read back identically to MzMLSqliteHandler::write_experiment of the same experiment (tier 4).",
    "IndexedMzMLFileLoader_test.cpp's VALIDATE_TMP_FILES step runs under the mzml-schema feature (libxml2 XSD validation of both written files).",
    "MSDataCachedConsumer (ported at wave-4 integration, INTEG-F, once lane F4's CachedMzMLHandler and lane F7a's consumers met): every START_SECTION of MSDataCachedConsumer_test.cpp is transcribed in tests/ms_data_cached_consumer.rs (tier 3). release_build_bytes streams MzMLFile_1.mzML through the consumer and requires the bytes of tests/data/f4_progress/MzMLFile_1.cached and empty.cached, which CachedMzMLHandler::writeMemdump wrote on the Linux x86_64 Release build (../oracle/F4-progress, ibminode06, openms4-release-bc9cc12-c19e494-174b576, two runs with the same sha256; see tests/data/f4_progress_provenance.json): writeMemdump (CachedMzMLHandler.cpp:33-58) and the consumer's constructor, consumeSpectrum, consumeChromatogram and destructor (MSDataCachedConsumer.cpp:18-75) write the same identifier, records and counts (tier 1 bytes, tier 4 equivalence).",
    "MSDataCachedConsumer, tier 1 (wave-4 integration): ../oracle/integ-F-cachedconsumer links the Linux x86_64 Release install openms4-release-bc9cc12-c19e494-174b576 on ibminode06 and runs the Release build's own MSDataCachedConsumer twice (identical files and records) over MzMLFile_1.mzML: every record with clearData, spectra 0 and 1 without it, nothing, and a spectrum after a chromatogram. tests/ms_data_cached_consumer.rs (release_consumer_*) requires the same four files byte for byte (tests/data/ms_data_cached_consumer/, verbatim), the same cleared or unchanged records, and the source's IllegalArgument message. The consumer's all-records file equals the writeMemdump output of ../oracle/F4-progress byte for byte."
  ],
  "gaps": [
    "MSDataAggregatingConsumer merges with a caller-supplied function: the source's SpectrumAddition::addUpSpectra(s_list, -1, true) (ANALYSIS/OPENSWATH/SpectrumAddition.h) is unported, and format may not depend on analysis. Its class test's 17/120/230 run with a merge double that adds intensities on the shared m/z grid.",
    "No tier 1 differential: no C++ oracle was run for these consumers.",
    "This manifest is not listed in SOURCE_PROVENANCE.json; registering it is the integrator's step."
  ],
